==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|годьныи}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*godьnъ}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-||to unite, be associated, suit}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|good}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|го́дный}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Cinemantique-годный.wav}}

===Adjective===
{{ru-adj|го́дный|+c'|годне́йший|adv=го́дно|absn=+,годнота́<qq:also an instance noun>}}

# [[fit]], [[suitable]], [[well]]-[[suited]], [[good]] for, [[valid]], [[appropriate]] {{+obj|ru|:для(gen)/:к(dat)/:на(acc)<for/to something>}}
# {{lb|ru|slang}} [[nice]], [[legit]]

====Usage notes====
The short form should not be conflated with the adjective {{m|ru|го́ден||fit for consumption}}, which has [[lexicalize]]d as a short-form-only adjective in its own right.

====Declension====
{{ru-decl-adj|го́дный|c'*}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|го́ден}}
* {{l|ru|го́дность}}
* {{l|ru|годнота́}}
* {{l|ru|приго́дный}}
